Week 2 - Linux Commands practiced in Labex.io with their uses

User and Group Information

echo → Displays a line of text or a variable value.
whoami → Displays the current username.
id → Shows detailed user and group information (UID, GID, groups).
sudo apt install htop → Installs the htop system monitoring tool.
htop → Interactive system monitor for processes and resource usage.

File Operations

cd → Changes the current working directory.
pwd → Displays the full path of the current working directory.
touch → Creates an empty file or updates the timestamp of an existing file.
mkdir → Creates a new directory.
ls → Lists the contents of a directory (use options like -l, -a, -h for more details).
cp → Copies files or directories.
mv → Moves or renames files and directories.
rm → Removes (deletes) files (be careful with this as it’s permanent).
rmdir → Removes empty directories.

